# Rust FFI Conventions

All C-facing exports live in `cdoom-core/src/ffi.rs` and follow cbindgen rules in `cbindgen.toml`.

## Naming and exports

- Public C functions use `#[no_mangle] pub extern "C"` with the `cdoom_rust_` prefix (configured in cbindgen).
- Return pointers to `'static` or process-lifetime data only — callers must not free them.
- Document `# Safety` on every `unsafe` block and every function returning raw pointers.

## Types

- Use `std::os::raw` C types (`c_int`, `c_char`, etc.) at the boundary.
- Set `usize_is_size_t = true` in cbindgen — do not use Rust `usize` in exported signatures.

## Adding a new export

1. Implement logic in a module under `cdoom-core/src/`.
2. Add a thin wrapper in `ffi.rs`.
3. Rebuild — cbindgen updates `include/cdoom_rust.h` automatically.
4. Wire the C caller with `#ifdef USE_RUST_<MODULE>` dual-run until parity passes.

```rust
// ✅ GOOD — static lifetime, documented
#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn cdoom_rust_version() -> *const c_char {
    version_cstr().as_ptr()
}

// ❌ BAD — caller would use-after-free
#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn cdoom_rust_version() -> *const c_char {
    CString::new("1.0").unwrap().as_ptr()
}
```
